Mix ingredients, except yeast extract, starch, sulfur and       Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O, and filter-sterilize while gassing with N<sub>2</sub>.      Autoclave yeast extract and starch as 10% solutions and       Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O as a 5% solution under a N<sub>2</sub> atmosphere.      Steam sulfur for 3 hr on each of       3 successive days.   Aseptically and anaerobically add the yeast       extract and starch solutions, and sulfur to the medium.      Prior to inoculation, add the sterile Na<sub>2</sub>S&#183;9H<sub>2</sub>O solution, and       adjust pH to 5.5 with sterile 1 N H<sub>2</sub>SO<sub>4</sub>.       <br>
